GAL16V8
BE6502DEC

A15  A14  A13  A12  A11  A10  PHI2 RW   NC   GND
NC   SIDCS ROMCE ACIACS LCDWR FMSEL NC  NC   NC   VCC

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; Ben Eater 6502 address decoder - replaces both 74HC138s and the 74HC00.
; Purely combinatorial. Assemble with galasm:  galasm BE6502DEC.pld
; (WinCUPL users want BE6502DEC_CUPL.PLD instead - different language.)
;
; $4800-$4BFF  SID / SIDKick pico   (kept, so existing software works)
; $4C00-$4FFF  LCD latch write strobe
; $5000-$53FF  W65C51 ACIA
; $5400-$57FF  FM select - the SKpico's OPL2, on its A8/IO pad
; $D400-$D7FF  SID again, native C64 address, so .sid files run unpatched
; ROM enabled for $8000-$FFFF EXCEPT the $D400 kilobyte
;
; RW is the 6502's R/W line: high = read, low = write.
; Still free: $4000-$47FF and $5800-$5FFF, plus three unused outputs.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

; $D400 = 1101 0100 ....   A15 A14 /A13 A12 /A11 A10
; $4800 = 0100 1000 ....  /A15 A14 /A13 /A12 A11 /A10
/SIDCS  =  A15 *  A14 * /A13 *  A12 * /A11 *  A10
        + /A15 *  A14 * /A13 * /A12 *  A11 * /A10

; $5000 = 0101 0000 ....  /A15 A14 /A13 A12 /A11 /A10
/ACIACS = /A15 *  A14 * /A13 *  A12 * /A11 * /A10

; $5400 = 0101 01.. ....  to the SKpico's A8/IO pad. With SID #2 set to FM
; at the IO address (config byte 8 = 4, byte 10 = 5) the SKpico takes the
; pad going low with its /CS high as an access to its OPL2. Its A5 pad -
; wired to CPU A5 already, for the $D420 second SID - must be high and
; A0-A3 low, and A4 picks the port: $5420 OPL2 address, $5430 OPL2 data.
; Address-only, like /SIDCS: the SKpico samples the bus itself.
/FMSEL  = /A15 *  A14 * /A13 *  A12 * /A11 *  A10

; $4C00 = 0100 1100 ....  qualified with PHI2 and WRITE.
; The 74LS574 clocks on a RISING edge, so this must go low during the
; access and rise at the end of it. Address decode alone will not do:
; the address bus is only guaranteed valid while PHI2 is high, and a
; transient through this 1K window between cycles would clock garbage
; into the latch. Every other device here qualifies internally or does
; not care - the latch is the only one that needs a clean edge.
/LCDWR  = /A15 *  A14 * /A13 * /A12 *  A11 *  A10 * PHI2 * /RW

; ROM on for A15=1, off across $D400-$D7FF. De Morgan on the exclusion:
; NOT(A14 * /A13 * A12 * /A11 * A10) = /A14 + A13 + /A12 + A11 + /A10
/ROMCE  =  A15 * /A14
        +  A15 *  A13
        +  A15 * /A12
        +  A15 *  A11
        +  A15 * /A10

DESCRIPTION

Five product terms is the widest equation here; a GAL16V8 gives eight per
output, so there is room to add selects as the machine grows. Eight of the ten
available inputs are used, and five of the eight outputs.

Pin 1 and pin 11 are inputs, which puts the part in simple mode. Note pins 15
and 16 have no feedback path in that mode - not needed here, but it matters if
outputs are ever fed back.
